:: JulesArrives {"title":"Chapter IV / An Exit with Benefits","scene":"kitchen"}
@action readCard() {
  @do $sawJobCard = true;
  @do $notes.push({id: $notes.length, text: "Jules offered Mars a legal fleet job with insurance and fixed hours."});
}

# An exit with benefits

@Chapter("CHAPTER IV · SUNDAY", "The successful nephew returns")

Jules arrives in a black car clean enough to insult the street. He sees Mars in your
lavender robe, the Sister Shift ledger, and his old jacket still hanging in the closet.

He needs only ten seconds.

::: dialogue {.dialogue speaker="Jules" mood="tired"}
“Auntie, you are committing crimes with nonprofit margins.”
:::

He slides a card toward Mars. A regional recovery fleet needs a driver. Legal wages.
Insurance. Fixed shifts. They check records, but Jules knows a manager.

@region jobCard {
  @if (!$sawJobCard) {
    [[Turn over the card => readCard]]
  } @else {
    @CaseFile("INTERVIEW", "MONDAY · 9:00 A.M.")
    @CaseFile("VEHICLE", "COMPANY OWNED · FULLY INSURED")
  }
}

Then Jules looks at you.

“Mars needs a job. You need Mars to need you. Those are not the same thing.”

After he leaves, the card remains on the table.

[[Tape it when Mars is not looking -> GiveCard]]

[[Put it in the trash and say nothing -> HideCard]]

[[Tell Mars you are afraid she'll take it -> ConfessFear]]

:: GiveCard {"title":"Chapter IV / Transparent Tape","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $honesty += 1
@do $trust += 1
@do $notes.push({id: $notes.length, text: "Lenora repaired the job card and left it beside Mars's coffee."})

@Chapter("MONDAY · 7:10 A.M.", "Transparent tape")

You tape the card together and leave it by Mars's mug. You also list six ways the
company probably exploits labor. Mars reads all six.

“You forgot number seven,” she says. “They expect me to arrive on time.”

[[Drive her to the interview -> InterviewMorning]]

:: HideCard {"title":"Chapter IV / The Private Archive","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $leverage += 3
@do $trust -= 2
@do $notes.push({id: $notes.length, text: "Lenora hid the job card in the same drawer as Mars's spare key."})

@Chapter("MONDAY · 7:10 A.M.", "The private archive")

You place the card in the drawer where you keep tax notices, spare keys, and things
you prefer to call evidence instead of secrets.

Mars dresses carefully anyway. Jules sent her the address before he came.

“I am meeting someone,” she says.

You can still decide what kind of person meets her at the door.

[[Give her the card and admit where it was -> LateConfession]]

[[Say nothing. Make a phone call after she leaves -> TheCall]]

:: ConfessFear {"title":"Chapter IV / A Sentence Without Armor","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $honesty += 3
@do $trust += 2
@do $notes.push({id: $notes.length, text: "Lenora admitted she was afraid of becoming unnecessary."})

@Chapter("MONDAY · 7:10 A.M.", "A sentence without armor")

“I am afraid you will find somewhere that does not need me,” you say.

Mars waits for the theory that will turn confession into weather. None comes.

“That is the first useful thing you have said all month.”

She pockets the card. “Come with me. Do not speak to the manager.”

[[Promise absolutely nothing and drive -> InterviewMorning]]

:: LateConfession {"title":"Chapter IV / Before the Truck Starts","scene":"yard"}
@do $honesty += 2
@do $trust -= 1
@do $notes.push({id: $notes.length, text: "Lenora confessed before sabotage could become a plan."})

@Chapter("MONDAY · 8:04 A.M.", "Before the truck starts")

You catch Mars at the curb. The taped card looks pathetic in your palm.

“I hid this.”

Mars looks from the card to you. “Did it work?”

“No.”

“Then get in. I need a ride.”

It is not forgiveness. It is transportation.

[[Drive in silence -> InterviewMorning]]

